=== 3. COMPILER BUILTIN TYPES ===

These types are defined in the Verus compiler (verus_builtin), not vstd:

Mathematical Types:
  int - Mathematical unbounded integer (can be negative)
  nat - Natural number (non-negative integer, >= 0)
  real - Mathematical real number (arbitrary precision)

Wrapper Types:
  Ghost<T> - Ghost wrapper - data exists only in proofs, erased at runtime
  Tracked<T> - Tracked wrapper - linear/affine data for permission tracking

Function Types:
  FnSpec - Specification-only function type (ghost callable)

Builtin Traits:
  Integer - Marker trait for integer types (int, nat, u8..u128, i8..i128)
  Chainable - Verus builtin trait
  Sealed - Sealed trait pattern - prevents external implementations

